--- body ---

## Context

The local machine has five possible reviewer runtimes: Mistral Vibe, Claude
Code, Pi, Aider and Codex. A runtime can expose several models and reasoning
effort settings, so counting CLI names is not a measure of independent review
coverage. The existing panel in `skills/reviewers/panel.yml` and its
`scripts/seat-runner.sh` execute sandboxed seats (see [[0205]]); the IDH
runtime-adapter programme [[0800]] covers Claude Code, Codex, Pi and Vibe.
This ticket audits the reviewer-seat choices across all five without
expanding the active roster by assumption.

On PR #1541 of climate-finance-het (2026-09-28), Vibe 2.25.8 was invoked
directly with `--agent ask -p` for a read-only review. It attempted a repo
write that the sandbox denied, then exited 0 after a partial reply rather
than returning findings. This is a concrete completion and containment probe,
not evidence that the runtime cannot review when configured correctly.

## Actions

1. Inventory the installed versions and callable reviewer modes for all five
   runtimes on doudou and padme. For each, record available model selectors,
   effort/reasoning controls, credential source by *name only*, and whether
   output can be made non-interactive and machine-readable. Distinguish CLI
   runtime, model provider and model: the same model through two CLIs is not
   two independent reviewers.
2. Compare each candidate mode with the existing seat-runner contract:
   read-only OS sandbox, scoped credentials, bounded cost/turns/time, no PR
   mutation, explicit non-zero/partial-result handling, and normalized
   `verifiable:` / `consider:` findings with file:line evidence. Reproduce
   and diagnose the Vibe partial-reply case.
3. Run bounded, read-only smoke probes on one frozen public PR diff for each
   viable runtime/model/effort combination chosen from the inventory (not the
   full Cartesian product). Record whether the seat actually reads the diff,
   returns a complete review, and leaves the checkout unchanged; compare
   latency, cost and distinct verified findings. Use the existing audition
   board when a candidate merits a broader trial.
4. Recommend a roster of at most four complementary advisory seats, or
   explain why the present roster should stay. Place implementation gaps in
   scoped follow-up tickets; do not silently promote a candidate to required.

## Evidence and exit criteria

- [ ] A versioned matrix names Vibe, Claude Code, Pi, Aider and Codex, their
      tested model/effort configurations, launch commands, host, limits,
      credential *variable names*, and pass/fail reasons.
- [ ] Each viable candidate has a reproducible, sandboxed smoke result with
      normalized findings or an explicit failure, plus a clean-worktree check.
- [ ] The Vibe PR #1541 partial reply is classified with a reproducer and a
      completion check that would reject an exit-0 non-review.
- [ ] The roster recommendation cites independence and cost/latency evidence
      and identifies the owner ticket for every gap left open.
- [ ] `erg check tickets` passes; no credential value or private PR content is
      committed to the audit artifacts.
